 ## Current constraints
 
+### Execution-routing integration boundary
+
+The Lane C selector persists and validates the frozen execution-routing settings schema, walks subscription-first routes in order, and returns a safe `resolved`, `approval_needed`, or `blocked` outcome. It does not yet launch an executor, resolve a credential, create a durable cdesktop approval for `meteredFallback=ask`, or recover a route swap after an executor boundary. Do not treat those integration behaviors as shipped.
+
+The standalone pool UI remains a loopback compatibility and recovery view for account-pool diagnostics only. cdesktop remains the primary visible workspace and session UI.
+
 ### Codex protocol boundary
 
 Upstream cdesktop 0.2.3 uses Codex app-server protocol types from Codex 0.121. An explicit `service_tier = "default"` in current Codex configuration causes that build to reject the thread-start response because its older enum understands only `fast` and `flex`.
