 Open cdesktop with `sightmesh service open`, select the migrated workspace, and create a Claude Code or Codex session. Before writing, read `.context/sightmesh-migration.json` when present and then read the referenced handoff. Context-only archived workspaces open their archived directory directly.
 
 Because the imported workspace uses the original checkout, do not resume the corresponding Conductor session after cutover. Keep one visible owner and one active tool per checkout.
+
+## Execution-routing upgrade note
+
+Execution routing is separate local policy. It does not migrate provider credentials, alter imported cdesktop sessions, or copy Conductor transcript state. After migration, keep launching and supervising work in cdesktop. Configure routes only after the operator-owned account pool is healthy, then use `sightmesh routing validate` and `sightmesh routing explain` to inspect the selector without launching work.
+
+The current selector does not yet execute a selected route or recover/approve a route swap in cdesktop. `sightmesh pool serve` remains a loopback compatibility view for account-pool diagnostics, not a primary session UI or approval surface.
