 `scripts/package-smoke.sh` builds standard source and wheel artifacts with `python -m build`, installs the wheel into an isolated virtual environment, verifies the `sightmesh` entry point and packaged migration command, and runs `twine check`.
 
 The compatibility workflow validates Python 3.11 through 3.13 and runs package smoke on each supported version. Tag releases build wheel and sdist artifacts, write SHA-256 checksums, use `actions/attest@v4` with GitHub OIDC provenance, and upload all artifacts to the matching GitHub release.
 
 GitHub artifact attestations provide signed Sigstore provenance for the published release assets. Publishing to PyPI or another package index remains a separate maintainer decision and is not performed by the release workflow.
+
+## Execution-routing release notes
+
+When release notes mention execution routing, describe only the shipped boundary:
+
+- frozen local settings schema version `1` under `executionRouting`;
+- subscription-first route ordering across `CODEX` and `CLAUDE_CODE` models;
+- `meteredFallback` values `auto`, `ask`, and `never`;
+- safe aliases and opaque `auth_binding_id` values only;
+- non-launching `show`, `validate`, `routes`, `set-metered`, and `explain` CLI behavior.
+
+Do not claim executor launch integration, durable cdesktop approval for `meteredFallback=ask`, route-swap recovery, credential resolution, or standalone pool UI routing. Those are integration boundaries for a later release. Keep examples secret-free and aligned with [execution routing](execution-routing.md) and [example settings](../examples/execution-routing.subscription-first.json).
